ent:",[490,1009,1010,1020],{},[493,1011,1012],{},[496,1013,1014,1017],{},[499,1015,1016],{},"Selection",[499,1018,1019],{},"Behavior",[510,1021,1022,1032,1042],{},[496,1023,1024,1029],{},[515,1025,1026],{},[255,1027,1028],{},"['*']",[515,1030,1031],{},"Access data from all tenants",[496,1033,1034,1039],{},[515,1035,1036],{},[255,1037,1038],{},"['tenant-123']",[515,1040,1041],{},"Access data from a single tenant",[496,1043,1044,1049],{},[515,1045,1046],{},[255,1047,1048],{},"['tenant-123', 'tenant-456']",[515,1050,1051],{},"Access data from multiple tenants",[247,1053,1055],{"id":1054},"security-considerations","Security Considerations",[243,1057,1058,1059,1063,1064,1066,1067,1069],{},"A participant that belongs to a tenant is confined to it. Through the admin repository, including its ",[636,1060,1062],{"href":1061},"\u002Fapps\u002Fpersistence\u002Fnamed-queries#admin-repository-queries","named queries",", it may select only its own tenant; naming another tenant, or ",[255,1065,1028],{},", is refused with an authorization error. On save, a blank ",[255,1068,257],{}," is filled with the participant's tenant and any other value is rejected. Selecting other tenants is possible only for a participant without a tenant, which is how a microservice in a project's deployment connects (organization scope), and such a participant must name the tenant of every entity it saves.",[243,1071,1072],{},"The standard tenant-isolated repository is the default and should be used for regular application logic.",[1074,1075,1076],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .s7zQu, html code.shiki .s7zQu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}htm